iteria?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":1,"explanation":"Independence requires a new example that still uses the taught skill. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Name price only, with no linked example","Create two invented lunch boxes with price, size and one durability fact","Retype the worked example with no new example","Choosing only by the biggest discount sticker"],"question":"Which independent response best applies criteria to new material?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"explanation":"Independent evidence on new material demonstrates the skill; copying the model does not.","marking_guide":"Accept original work about criteria with a specific supporting detail. Reject copied model wording with no new material.","question":"Produce a fresh example demonstrating criteria on new material (not the worked model). Explain the particular words, sources or choices that make it work.","sample_answer":"Sample: original example using criteria on new material; names a specific word, source or choice and explains its effect.","type":"short_answer"},{"explanation":"A useful correction changes the inaccurate idea or method and explains why.","marking_guide":"Accept a misconception, a correction, and a purpose-linked reason for criteria. Reject corrections that do not change the inaccurate idea.","question":"Name one likely error with criteria, correct it, and explain why the correction helps a reader or audience.","sample_answer":"Sample error: Choosing only by the biggest discount sticker.. Correction: Pack B. A snapped lead fails the purpose. The difference is $5 − $3 = $2. Cheapest fails when the criterion is a. Why it helps the audience is stated.","type":"short_answer"}],"resources":null,"response_prompt":"Include your independent evidence and reflection, with reasons where requested.","review_status":"unreviewed","seed_key":"s5-commerce-y9-w03-l1","sort_activity":null,"source_note":"Proposed Year 7 Commerce alignment to Commerce 7–10 (2024) outcome CO5-DEC-01. The syllabus says Stage 4 may adjust Stage 5 outcomes (CO4-ADJ-01). Content-point mapping pending. Not NESA verified. Not financial advice.","spelling":null,"spelling_focus":null,"stage":"S4","stage_hints":{"accept":["Today you will practise criteria.","Read the mission before you start mapping or using sources.","Keep the place, people or source you are studying in view."],"guided":["Attempt the guided prompt without looking ahead.","Afterwards, compare your evidence with the feedback.","Adjust anything that does not match the method."],"learn":["Study how the first demonstration is built.","Point to the source or place detail that carries the idea.","Then write the reason without copying every sentence."],"quiz":["Read every option before you choose.","Eliminate answers that ignore sources or respectful practice.","Prefer accurate evidence over a guess that merely looks neat."],"submit":["Confirm that your evidence and reason are both present.","Proofread names, places, dates and sequence.","Make sure the final evidence matches the lesson purpose."],"teach0":["Read the stage title and find the worked model.","Name one exact source detail or place feature before you decide.","Try the small prompt before opening the comparison."],"teach1":["Return to the model and list the key evidence.","Say what each source or place detail shows about the idea.","A final label alone is weaker than recorded evidence."],"teach2":["Compare a weak claim with stronger evidence.","Change the claim or use of sources, not only how neat the poster looks.","Name the mistake you are repairing."],"teach3":["Choose a fresh place, person or source that still uses the same skill.","Write one reason in your own words.","Do not retype the worked model as your answer."],"write":["Follow every part of the independent instructions.","Include original evidence and a short reason.","Save work that shows the skill on new sources or places."]},"subject":"Commerce","success_criteria":["I can use criteria with a specific example from this lesson.","I can identify price and explain why it matters.","I can practise purpose independently on a new prompt.","I can notice durability needs and correct a likely mistake."],"suspense_builder":null,"teach_steps":[{"check":{"correct_index":3,"explanation":"Comparing products needs criteria decided before you look at the brighter packet.","options":["A claim unrelated to the source or place","An answer copied without understanding","A guess with no evidence","Comparing products needs criteria decided before you look at the brighter packet"],"question":"Which choice best shows accurate use of this idea about criteria?","type":"multiple_choice"},"example":"WORKED MODEL\nBottle North: $12, 600 mL, lid cracked in the shop sample. Bottle South: $16, 750 mL, intact lid, thicker wall. If the criterion “must last the term” ranks above “cheapest”, South fits better even though it costs $4 more. $16 − $12 = $4.\n\nTRY FIRST\nCompare Pencil Pack A ($3, leads snap in the packet) and Pack B ($5, leads intact, 12 pencils). Which is the better buy if the criterion is “works for a month of homework”, and what is the price difference?\n\nFEEDBACK\nPack B. A snapped lead fails the purpose. The difference is $5 − $3 = $2. Cheapest fails when the criterion is a working pencil, not the lowest tag.","explain":"Comparing products needs criteria decided before you look at the brighter packet. Useful criteria for a water bottle are price, purpose (does it hold a school day’s water) and durability (will the lid still seal after a month). Invented classroom products are enough. You do not need a real brand, and a brand name is not evidence of quality.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\nThis helps the learner base claims on sources, places and respectful community knowledge, rather than guessing from a single picture. Keep every claim linked to evidence.\n\nHOW TO WORK\nRead the worked example and name the sources, map features or community examples that carry the idea. Before looking at the correction, make your own attempt using the exact question provided. Compare your record with the feedback: did you use the same skill and show your evidence? If a detail is uncertain, identify what source you would need next. One deliberate, evidence-based revision is more useful than writing a longer answer.","icon":"📖","notice":"Choosing only by the biggest discount sticker. A discount on an item that does not do the job is still a poor buy. Correct the claim or use of sources, not just the neatness of the poster.","title":"Understand and model","visual":[{"alt":"The dearer bottle has the lid that still seals.","caption":"Durability can outrank the lower price.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">North $12</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">cracked lid</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">South $16</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">lid intact</text></g></svg>"}],"visual_before":[{"episode":{"scenes":[{"bg":"room","lines":[{"text":"I can see the example, but I am not sure which source or place detail matters most.","who":"pip"},{"text":"Name the sources, map features or community examples that carry the idea before you decide.","who":"juno"},{"text":"I will try the prompt myself, then compare with the feedback.","who":"pip"},{"pause_after":true,"text":"Pause here. Use this model: Bottle North: $12, 600 mL, lid cracked in the shop sample. Bottle South: $16, 750 mL, intact lid, thicker wall. If the c Then write your own evidence.","who":"juno"}]}],"title":"Talk through the first model","transcript":"Pip: I can see the example, but I am not sure which source or place detail matters most.\nJuno: Name the sources, map features or 